Copyright and license notices for the third-party code bundled in dt2
=====================================================================

The dt2 Python package (Python code and the anywidget adapter in js/) is
copyright of the package authors and distributed under the MIT license (see
LICENSE). It is a Python port of the R package DT2.

dt2 is a binding: the table engine is third-party work. Rendering, ordering,
searching, paging and every extension are done by DataTables, a JavaScript
library developed by SpryMedia Ltd (https://datatables.net). The wheel and
the sdist ship a pre-built bundle, src/dt2/static/index.js and index.css,
produced with esbuild from the npm packages pinned in package-lock.json; it
contains DataTables and the libraries listed below, unmodified apart from
minification. Each of them remains the copyright of its authors and is used
under its own license.

dt2 is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by or
endorsed by SpryMedia Ltd or by any of the other projects listed here.

